        position: "**India's largest video-surveillance brand, with 43.3% of the market in FY26** (Frost & Sullivan), roughly double its earlier share, and by its own account one of the largest CCTV factories in the world.",
        money: "Net debt of about ₹56cr on Screener; the company puts debt at just 0.07 times equity after its August 2025 IPO, which helped cut borrowings from ₹509cr to ₹256cr. Capex rose to ₹136cr in FY26 and will continue as capacity doubles. Operating cash flow is thin (₹13cr in FY26) because stock and receivables grow with sales. Promoters hold **74.7%**, down from 77.1% in September 2025.",
        watch: ["Whether the roughly 25% price rises stick without losing buyers.", "Margin holding in the guided 14-15% range as memory costs rise.", "Any change to the rule barring Chinese chips from CCTV."],
